Healers are very vulnerable in the early game. But they have a couple
of options that they should make use of; one very important one is the
healing spell. Metal armour can have a great impact on spell success
(see http://nh.gridbug.de/spells.html to play with the parameters).
With their starting wisdom of around 16 they may fail with the healing
spell, and this can be crucial in the early game. Note that typically
you will find also metal hats and metal boots, and with those and GOP
your level 1 healing spell will fail with 55% probability. Removing
either boots and helm, or GOP, will make that only 6% failure; still
not reliable but you may decide whether it's worth or not. You should
note that iron helm and iron boots are primarily a defensive means,
while GOP support offensive success, and a 0% healing spell may save
your life if offence or defence actions have been ineffective. So you
have to weigh the pros and cons depending on the game evolution and
the concrete situation.

